  "title": "SpaceX Launches AI Data Centers and FCC Approves Satellite Deployment",
  "summary": "NASA is advancing American leadership in space by taking the next step toward a future where commercial space stations lead the way in low Earth orbit. On Friday, the agency released its final Request for Proposals inviting industry to submit plans for the next generation of commercial space stations. The FCC has authorized SpaceX to deploy up to 1 million AI chip-equipped satellites as part of the Elon Musk-owned company's 'Starmind' initiative. With several others also pursuing the idea of putting AI data centers in space, including Google and Blue Origin, this is the first approval the agency [&#8230;].",
